{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q83036064","formula":"C₂₀H₂₃N₃","hill":"C20H23N3","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":23.0,"N":3.0},"names":{"en":"LEK 8829"},"descriptions":{"en":"LEK-8829, also known as desoxy-LEK-8842, is a non-selective monoamine receptor modulator of the ergoline family related to the psychedelic drug LSD which has been studied as a potential novel antipsychotic. It is an analogue of LSD in which the oxygen atom of the carboxamide moiety has been removed to instead form an aminomethyl moiety, along with different amine substitutions (methyl and propynyl instead of diethyl). The drug acts as a dopamine D1 receptor agonist, dopamine D2 receptor antagonist, and serotonin 5-HT1A and 5-HT2A receptor antagonist, among other actions."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":9796528,"mass":305.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1C[C@@H](C=C2[C@H]1CC3=CNC4=CC=CC2=C34)CN(C)CC#C","inchikey":"YBCGYAGNYOYLDH-IFXJQAMLSA-N","iupac":"N-[[(6aR,9S)-7-methyl-6,6a,8,9-tetrahydro-4H-indolo[4,3-fg]quinolin-9-yl]methyl]-N-methylprop-2-yn-1-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"9796528","atoms":46,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.601,"y":-2.18,"z":0.102,"el":"N"},{"x":-5.068,"y":-0.223,"z":0.231,"el":"N"},{"x":4.332,"y":-0.144,"z":-0.569,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.581,"y":-1.335,"z":0.43,"el":"C"},{"x":1.89,"y":-0.267,"z":-0.796,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.506,"y":0.087,"z":-0.199,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.897,"y":-2.11,"z":0.047,"el":"C"},{"x":1.849,"y":-1.411,"z":0.23,"el":"C"},{"x":0.619,"y":0.538,"z":-0.78,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.729,"y":0.92,"z":-0.158,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.081,"y":-1.212,"z":0.112,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.909,"y":0.183,"z":0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":3.101,"y":0.628,"z":-0.53,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.151,"y":0.793,"z":0.072,"el":"C"},{"x":0.68,"y":-3.375,"z":0.948,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.429,"y":-1.444,